From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 15:53:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: health HAL to AIDL

android.hardware.health@2.1 is gone from every framework compatibility
matrix in the tree (AIDL IHealth only, FCM 7 upward), so the HIDL service
fails check_vintf_compatible. Rebuild the device implementation on
hardware/interfaces/health/aidl/default (libhealth_aidl_impl), the same
shape as newer Pixels: Health subclass with UpdateHealthInfo plus the
eMMC getStorageInfo/getDiskStats, one binary that is also the charger
(--charger, charger_vendor domain), replacing /system/bin/charger.

The two device helpers (BatteryRechargingControl, BatteryInfoUpdate) take
the AIDL HealthInfo now; they only read and write batteryStatus and
batteryLevel, whose values are the same. libpixelhealth already carries
HealthInfo overloads for everything else.
